    "name": "varcoeff_laplacian_x_dirichlet_bc_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_x_dirichlet_bc: a minimal consuming model binding NX=NY=4 at the import edge. The compound match D( k * D(u,x), x ) fires (priority 10) through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint and lowers to the rule's makearray -- the interior conservative flux-difference stencil aggregate over u and k, plus the two x-edge faces over the singleton-x full-rank strips -- with zero apply_expression_template nodes, zero surviving spatial D, and the free names (gL, gR, dx) surviving in the expanded body. The coefficient k is a consumer-supplied [x,y]-shaped field (here k=1+0.5 cos(2 pi x_gi), constant in y), bound by the match as the LEFT factor of the product; u is the state. x0=y0=0 and dx=dy=1/4 spelled with the literal 4 because the edge binding closes NX/NY before this document's scope (grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "ast",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "rule:varcoeff_laplacian_x_dirichlet_bc"
    ]
  },
